{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017G1iEvMJ88Vj7XifjohRTb","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the information about the StreamsConfig property headers-aware DSL stores name change and reviewer feedback from 2026-02-22.\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\\\n\\\\nThe StreamsConfig property for the headers-aware DSL stores was changed from **`dsl.store.type`** to **`dsl.store.format`** based on reviewer feedback.\\\\n\\\\n**Reviewer feedback and change:**\\\\n\\\\n- **Reviewer:** Lucas Brutschy (feedback on 2026-02-20)\\\\n- **Feedback point (LB1):** Suggested that the config name `dsl.store.type` felt ambiguous since it could be confused with `dsl.store.suppliers.class` (which controls RocksDB vs. in-memory). Proposed `dsl.store.format` as clearer, since this is really about the value format (timestamped vs. timestamped+headers).\\\\n\\\\n- **Author response:** Alieh Saeedi acknowledged on 2026-02-22: \\\\\\\"dsl.store.type makes sense to me, but I'm not attached to it. I can change it (and already have changed it) to dsl.store.format if we prefer that naming.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis discussion was part of **KIP-1285: DSL Opt-in Support for Header-Aware State Stores**, which proposes adding DSL-level opt-in support for headers-aware stores introduced in KIP-1271.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/02/22/mail-c4bfde361f38ca346dffd233-ed6480b7.md` (Alieh Saeedi's response with the name change acknowledgment)\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/02/22/mail-6ea3402c8bc00ae4fb37dcf5-d5ef6d28.md` (Matthias J. Sax's additional feedback on the same topic)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/02/22/mail-6ea3402c8bc00ae4fb37dcf5-d5ef6d28.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/02/22/mail-c4bfde361f38ca346dffd233-ed6480b7.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":19.62,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":2,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":82200,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":12262,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.040647,\\\"input_tokens\\\":58,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1569}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9212642-08de-481d-b2a4-57ce10d1f2f6","uuid":"3158707a-c654-4761-b5f9-65c48f59e361","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:55:14.746Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the information about the StreamsConfig property headers-aware DSL stores name change and reviewer feedback from 2026-02-22.\\\\n\\\\n## Answer\\\\n\\\\nThe StreamsConfig property for the headers-aware DSL stores was changed from **`dsl.store.type`** to **`dsl.store.format`** based on reviewer feedback.\\\\n\\\\n**Reviewer feedback and change:**\\\\n\\\\n- **Reviewer:** Lucas Brutschy (feedback on 2026-02-20)\\\\n- **Feedback point (LB1):** Suggested that the config name `dsl.store.type` felt ambiguous since it could be confused with `dsl.store.suppliers.class` (which controls RocksDB vs. in-memory). Proposed `dsl.store.format` as clearer, since this is really about the value format (timestamped vs. timestamped+headers).\\\\n\\\\n- **Author response:** Alieh Saeedi acknowledged on 2026-02-22: \\\\\\\"dsl.store.type makes sense to me, but I'm not attached to it. I can change it (and already have changed it) to dsl.store.format if we prefer that naming.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis discussion was part of **KIP-1285: DSL Opt-in Support for Header-Aware State Stores**, which proposes adding DSL-level opt-in support for headers-aware stores introduced in KIP-1271.\\\\n\\\\n**Files cited:**\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/02/22/mail-c4bfde361f38ca346dffd233-ed6480b7.md` (Alieh Saeedi's response with the name change acknowledgment)\\\\n- `/store/_intake/2026/02/22/mail-6ea3402c8bc00ae4fb37dcf5-d5ef6d28.md` (Matthias J. Sax's additional feedback on the same topic)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/02/22/mail-6ea3402c8bc00ae4fb37dcf5-d5ef6d28.md\\\",\\\"_intake/2026/02/22